## Purpose

`/checkin` catches what's visible every morning. `/audit` catches what's invisible — commitments Christopher made in Slack that never became Trello cards, action items from meetings that were never logged, cards that have gone stale without anyone noticing.

This skill exists because the insights report (Feb 2026) identified **32 "missing information" friction events** as the single largest friction category. Many of these were tasks that existed in Slack conversations but not in any task system. `/checkin` Stage 4 does a lightweight daily cross-reference; `/audit` does the full 7-day reconciliation.

**Recommended cadence:** Weekly, Monday mornings before the family meal. Can also be run ad-hoc when Christopher feels things are slipping through cracks.

**This is NOT `/checkin`.** `/checkin` is a fast daily briefing (60-90 seconds). `/audit` is a thorough integrity check (3-5 minutes). Don't substitute one for the other.

