## Execution Protocol

### Stage 1: Snapshot Current State (Trello)

**Gate:** Cannot proceed without reading ALL active Trello lists.

**Execution:**

1. Fetch all cards from the three active lists via Trello API:

```bash
# Review (inbox)
curl -s "https://api.trello.com/1/lists/${TRELLO_LIST_REVIEW}/cards?key=${TRELLO_API_KEY}&token=${TRELLO_TOKEN}&fields=name,desc,dateLastActivity,labels,due"

# Action (committed work)
curl -s "https://api.trello.com/1/lists/${TRELLO_LIST_ACTION}/cards?key=${TRELLO_API_KEY}&token=${TRELLO_TOKEN}&fields=name,desc,dateLastActivity,labels,due"

# Waiting (blocked on others)
curl -s "https://api.trello.com/1/lists/${TRELLO_LIST_WAITING}/cards?key=${TRELLO_API_KEY}&token=${TRELLO_TOKEN}&fields=name,desc,dateLastActivity,labels,due"
```

2. Build a deduplicated index of every active card:

```yaml
card_index:
  - name: "[card title]"
    id: "[card id]"
    list: "[Review | Action | Waiting]"
    owner: "[extracted from name prefix, e.g. 'Christopher']"
    last_activity: "[ISO date]"
    days_since_activity: [N]
    due: "[ISO date or null]"
    overdue: [true/false]
    status: "[active | stale | at_risk]"
```

3. Flag any card not updated in 5+ days as `stale`
4. Flag any card not updated in 14+ days as `at_risk`
5. Flag any card with a past due date as `overdue`

