**CRITICAL:** Do NOT auto-apply changes. Present the report and wait for Christopher to approve, cherry-pick, or reject.

**Applying approved changes:**

For new cards:
```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://api.trello.com/1/cards" \
  -d "key=${TRELLO_API_KEY}" \
  -d "token=${TRELLO_TOKEN}" \
  -d "idList=${TRELLO_LIST_REVIEW}" \
  -d "name=Owner: Card title" \
  -d "desc=Source: /audit — [date]
Context: [commitment text and source]"
```

For moving to Done:
```bash
curl -s -X PUT "https://api.trello.com/1/cards/[CARD_ID]" \
  -d "key=${TRELLO_API_KEY}" \
  -d "token=${TRELLO_TOKEN}" \
  -d "idList=${TRELLO_LIST_DONE}"
```

For archiving:
```bash
curl -s -X PUT "https://api.trello.com/1/cards/[CARD_ID]" \
  -d "key=${TRELLO_API_KEY}" \
  -d "token=${TRELLO_TOKEN}" \
  -d "closed=true"
```

**Card naming conventions:**
- Lead with owner prefix: `Christopher:`, `Jason:`, `Stanley:`, `Ben:`, etc.
- One action = one card. Sub-steps go in the card description, not as separate cards.
- Title should be specific enough to act on without opening the card.

